1
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,800
Ace, Luffy, Listen!

2
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:21,064
The three of us, we're
gonna leave this country!

3
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:24,500
We're gonna sail the seas
and see the whole world!

4
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:29,240
From now on, we're
honest-to-goodness brothers.

5
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:30,520
Cheers to that!

6
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,630
Brothers!

7
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:55,782
How long are you going to
lay there like a moron?

8
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:00,857
By the way, the treasure we were
keeping in the forest is gone.

9
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:02,437
Someone must have gotten to it.

10
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:04,696
Meh, I don't care about the treasure.

11
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:05,890
Not anymore.

12
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:09,457
I mean, those were pirate
savings I was sharing with Sabo.

13
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:11,422
And you, too, later on, I guess.

14
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:14,622
But in the end, he didn't
need money to set sail.

15
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,565
So why should I get bent
out of shape about it?

16
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:22,531
After all, what's the point in having
treasure if you can't even protect it?

17
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:24,700
Hey, Ace!

18
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:26,910
I...

19
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:30,240
I wanna get stronger!

20
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:50,737
be the strongest in the world and then

21
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:54,617
I'll protect everyone I will lose Anyone

22
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:58,917
I care about you gotta make me a promise

23
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,800
I'm begging you please
don't Don't die, Gaze!

24
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:04,940
Cut it out.

25
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:08,584
You ought to be worried
about dying before I do.

26
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:11,437
What, did you forget you're
a lot weaker than me?

27
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:13,344
Listen, and you listen up good.

28
00:02:14,820 --> 00:02:16,420
I'm never going to die.

29
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:24,169
You know, Sabo told me
to take care of you.

30
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:28,240
So I promise, I'm not
gonna die, okay? Not ever.

31
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:33,937
At least not as long as I've got a wussy
little brother who needs me to protect him.

32
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:34,850
Yeah, okay.

33
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:37,797
Smarts aren't exactly my strong point,

34
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:41,500
so I still don't really
understand why Sabo was killed.

35
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,640
But whoever did it,

36
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:46,617
they must be opposed
to freedom because they

37
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:49,465
shot him down before he
ever got a taste of it.

38
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:54,660
But we shared that same cup of sake
with him, and we're still alive.

39
00:02:58,140 --> 00:03:00,057
Luffy, listen to me, okay?

40
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:05,000
There's just one way to live
and that's without any regrets.

41
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:23,377
Boys from families like
mine once they turn

42
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:26,000
18 they're officially
registered as nobles.

43
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:28,377
That's why I'm leaving.

44
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:30,500
I gotta be gone before I'm 17.

45
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:35,050
Someday.

46
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:38,260
We're gonna set sail just like Sabo.

47
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:40,757
We're gonna live the way we wanna live.

48
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,960
More free than anyone else.

49
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:47,457
But you know what that means?

50
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:49,997
We'll make plenty of
enemies along the way.

51
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:52,697
We're gonna have to
fight Garp someday I bet.

52
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:55,317
We gotta be willing to risk everything.

53
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:59,180
Let's go out to sea at 17,
just like Sabo planned.

54
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:01,820
Then, we'll be pirates.

55
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:28,020
I love you.

56
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:58,017
Oh I know what I'm supposed to do?

57
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:06,180
Don't let go down, don't be able to shine!

58
00:05:17,593 --> 00:05:18,423
The battle of the world
is the end of the world!

59
00:05:18,506 --> 00:05:20,349
I am not going to hurt you, but
I don't want to do anything?

60
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:26,637
If you open the door, you
will be able to open the door.

61
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:31,780
Let's start with the new world.

62
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,000
We fight together.

63
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:32,750
I believe.

64
00:06:32,833 --> 00:06:39,577
I will connect to the future.

65
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:44,017
I will never be able to see you.

66
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:48,897
I will never be able to forget.

67
00:06:48,980 --> 00:06:51,840
Don't forget, we fight together.

68
00:06:58,020 --> 00:07:01,477
The world noble's visit to the
Goa Kingdom has come and gone.

69
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:06,697
But another visitor lingers at a
small village in the East Blue.

70
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:11,280
A group of aspiring swordsmen
chat about the strange encounter.

71
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:26,137
Did you see that weird guy
with the big head? Yes.

72
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,957
Face was totally crazy too.

73
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:31,275
I I bet he needs that giant
ship to fit his giant head.

74
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:36,300
580, 581,

75
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:41,560
582, 583, 584.

76
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:48,357
You certainly kept me waiting.

77
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:51,480
What could possibly be
more important than me?

78
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:54,410
Sorry.

79
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:56,550
Oh, goodness.

80
00:07:56,660 --> 00:07:57,537
Is that...

81
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:58,740
Someone get help.

82
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,317
This doesn't look good.

83
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:01,657
Let's prepare treatment.

84
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:02,570
Roger.

85
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:08,694
Honestly, what in the world
have you been up to all day?

86
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:12,512
I was watching the ceremony
they held for the World Noble.

87
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:13,970
Ah!

88
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:18,444
One, that's some risky business,
and two, why didn't you take me?

89
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:22,634
Because you would attract too
much attention, obviously.

90
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:25,420
Could it be I'm too fabulous?

91
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:29,520
At any rate, we've
tarried for long enough.

92
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,882
We've got business to attend to.

93
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:34,620
Do we have supplies?

94
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:38,497
The training hall at the village
gave us just enough food for now.

95
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:39,410
Very well.

96
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,400
Set sail.

97
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:45,100
We're heading back to Baltico.

98
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:55,100
A short time later, in
the nearby Goa Kingdom.

99
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:01,670
Ah!

100
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:03,080
Finally, some junk!

101
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:09,540
Although the fire raised Grey
Terminal and its people to the ground,

102
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:13,380
another sea of trash and another
sea of scavengers appeared.

103
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:20,600
You're in for it this time!

104
00:09:20,820 --> 00:09:21,860
Here it goes!

105
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:23,700
Now go! Go!

106
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:26,330
Pistol!

107
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:42,240
Are you kidding me?

108
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:43,780
You still suck butt.

109
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:49,817
It doesn't matter how hard you
punch if you can't hit anything.

110
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:52,060
I told you, rubber's a crappy power.

111
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:53,789
It's no good for fighting.

112
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:55,980
Shut up! You're dumb!

113
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,197
You're the dumb one!

114
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:58,640
I'm honest, that's all!

115
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:02,837
I'm trying to save you from falling
on your stupid rubber ass all day!

116
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:05,977
You're just jealous because you
can't do all some stuff like me!

117
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:10,297
All you've got are jerk powers and I'm
working on all kinds of cool moves!

118
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:12,197
Luffy, that was great!

119
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:17,440
Man, that punch of yours flies further
and further every day! Come on!

120
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,897
If you go easy on him,
he'll get a big head!

121
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:23,377
I got stronger today and I'm
gonna be even stronger tomorrow!

122
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:24,460
Right, Sabo?

123
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:44,809
This Abba was a nice
brother, not like you.

124
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:48,372
You're trying to say it'd be
better if I died, aren't you?

125
00:10:55,900 --> 00:10:57,160
Ow. Huh?

126
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:09,760
I'm hereby establishing my own country.

127
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:11,660
He's doing what now?

128
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:26,837
What are you little idiots up to now?

129
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:29,777
We need to be strong
enough to live on our own!

130
00:11:29,860 --> 00:11:31,877
You're from the Dadan kingdom, by the way.

131
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:34,680
We still need to use your bath though.

132
00:11:58,800 --> 00:11:59,630
Ahhhh...

133
00:11:59,713 --> 00:12:03,160
Ace, this one is way too
big, I need your help! You?

134
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,780
The mighty King Luffy needs help?

135
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:09,800
Here goes!

136
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:20,930
No!

137
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:36,200
Hey, it's the Dawn Kingdom! We need help!

138
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,540
Luffy got hurt!

139
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:38,760
He's in trouble!

140
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:41,930
Magra!

141
00:12:42,013 --> 00:12:43,540
Hurry up! This is bad!

142
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:45,240
Okay, Ace.

143
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:46,812
Hurry, bring him inside.

144
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:00,240
Okay, wow.

145
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:02,937
It's a good thing you brought
him here when you did.

146
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:07,667
Also, if this cut had been any deeper,
he probably would have died on the spot.

147
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:12,711
I hate to say it, but this is
no good with only two of you.

148
00:13:14,820 --> 00:13:16,100
It's all my fault.

149
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,360
I knew better.

150
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:23,256
Even if you're a captain, fighting
alone doesn't make you any stronger.

151
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:26,460
I'm still no good.

152
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:29,120
I'm still not good enough.

153
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:33,840
No, no.

154
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:36,160
I'm sorry, Luffy.

155
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:39,360
I let you down.

156
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:50,060
Guys, come see!

157
00:13:50,820 --> 00:13:53,640
Makino came to visit,
and she brought booze!

158
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:57,865
You want to know how to
properly say thank you?

159
00:13:58,660 --> 00:13:59,490
Mm-hmm.

160
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:02,055
And what's this about paying respects?

161
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:04,157
As a pirate and as Luffy's big brother,

162
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:07,060
I need to pay my respects
to this Shanks guy.

163
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:11,755
Luffy says he owes the man his life,
so it's kind of the least I can do.

164
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:22,200
Got something to say to me?

165
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:25,280
Sorry, sorry.

166
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:28,014
Okay, I think I can give you some tips.

167
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:30,397
For starters, after a meal...

168
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:32,380
It's a dining dish!

169
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:33,800
Come back!

170
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:38,640
Wait a sec, we almost forgot.

171
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:40,880
Gotta pay respect. Oops!

172
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:42,278
Yeah, you're right!

173
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:44,590
Oh?

174
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:47,147
Thank you for the meal, sir.

175
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:49,340
Ah! Keep your thanks!

176
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:51,559
Are you brats gonna pay me or what?

177
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,920
I'm not losing today! No way!

178
00:15:32,060 --> 00:15:34,137
All right, now it's time to go!

179
00:15:34,220 --> 00:15:35,867
Now for some bare meat stew!

180
00:17:04,220 --> 00:17:05,960
Take care, Ace. See ya!

181
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:07,630
Yeah!

182
00:17:07,713 --> 00:17:08,543
See you soon!

183
00:17:08,626 --> 00:17:09,760
Keep training hard!

184
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:13,157
Just give me three years
and before you know it,

185
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,946
my wanted poster's gonna
be everywhere you go!

186
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,320
Kick some ass!

187
00:17:23,580 --> 00:17:24,500
Bon voyage!

188
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:28,340
Don't catch a cold out there!

189
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:30,117
Look for me in the papers.

190
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,671
It won't take long, okay?

191
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:38,455
The world did not know that the son
of Gol Roger had grown up in secret,

192
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:43,400
nor did they know that he set sail that
day, determined to make a name of his own.

193
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:00,700
Yes, that's it, huh?

194
00:18:02,140 --> 00:18:05,380
Honestly, if Garp were here,
think of what he'd say.

195
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:27,080
Gonna need you to raise
this baby for me. What? Why?

196
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:28,460
Is it even yours?

197
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,557
So there you are, boss.

198
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:34,757
Hey, believe it or not, Ace is gone.

199
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:37,277
That's so well.

200
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:39,257
One last brat to worry about, though.

201
00:18:39,340 --> 00:18:41,177
I'm sure Garp will give me hell for it.

202
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:43,497
Kid left, and he's still
causing me trouble.

203
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:45,597
Oh, I almost forgot.

204
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:47,837
There's a message he
asked us to give to you.

205
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,537
Yeah, why should I care?

206
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:52,477
He probably just wants to tell
me my feet smell or something.

207
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:55,920
He said, thank you for taking care of me.

208
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:03,720
How could you do that to me, you beast?

209
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:06,677
What's wrong, boss?

210
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:08,077
You're not crying, are you?

211
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:10,513
If you don't shut up, I'll make you cry!

212
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:25,280
Three more years, that's the rule!

213
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:28,700
Now gum-gum-pistol!

214
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:33,500
So close!

215
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:35,620
I just need a little more!

216
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:39,520
You almost got it now, Luffy.

217
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:42,685
Bend your legs a little
and aim straight ahead.

218
00:19:46,260 --> 00:19:49,540
Now gum-gum-pistol!

219
00:20:02,860 --> 00:20:04,840
Gotta keep getting stronger!

220
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:06,820
Hang on, Ace!

221
00:20:07,100 --> 00:20:08,680
I'm coming for you!

222
00:20:16,780 --> 00:20:17,700
Luffy!

223
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:20,420
Hey, you gotta see the paper, look.

224
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:21,680
Oh, what's up?

225
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:23,153
It's just like he said.

226
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,420
Whoa, you're right, Ace made the news.

227
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:29,017
He's got a ship and a crew and everything.

228
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:31,680
Oh man, I'm so jealous, wow.

229
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:36,160
But I'm gonna do even better.

230
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:46,617
Hey, you guys!

231
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:50,000
I'm leaving now, you're
not gonna see me off? Hey!

232
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:52,620
Use your head for once.

233
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:55,597
The mayor and Makino
wouldn't mind us stopping by,

234
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:57,817
but as for everyone else
in Windmill Village,

235
00:20:57,900 --> 00:21:00,217
we'd probably scare the
pants right off them.

236
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,477
I don't know...

237
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:04,148
Ugh, don't make it
awkward, just go already!

238
00:21:04,520 --> 00:21:05,350
Okay.

239
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:07,000
Well, goodbye, you guys!

240
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,534
Thanks for everything!

241
00:21:08,660 --> 00:21:09,937
I'm sure gonna miss you!

242
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:11,217
Oh, now don't say that!

243
00:21:11,300 --> 00:21:12,757
You're gonna make us blush!

244
00:21:12,840 --> 00:21:14,740
Well, bye! Take it easy!

245
00:21:15,080 --> 00:21:16,000
I will!

246
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:17,360
You guys too, okay?

247
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:20,460
Oh, one last thing!

248
00:21:20,940 --> 00:21:24,000
Dad, I still think mountain
bandits are super lame!

249
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:25,889
Shut up and leave, dammit!

250
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:29,400
But you guys, you're great!

251
00:21:33,020 --> 00:21:35,040
It's not enough to ruin my life.

252
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:37,259
Now you got to break my heart, too.

253
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:38,980
You're awful, I tell you.

254
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:41,002
All of you are good for nothing.

255
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:43,600
Sorry I made you cry.

256
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:45,600
Shut up or I'll make you cry.

257
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:52,700
Now to Windmill Village on Dawn
Island at the edge of the Goa Kingdom.

258
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:56,857
No offense, but why don't you take
my old fishing boat instead, Luffy?

259
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:59,657
That thing is going to sink
as soon as you get out to sea.

260
00:21:59,740 --> 00:22:01,680
That's too small, even for you.

261
00:22:02,140 --> 00:22:05,434
I want to start small, but
I'll get a real big one soon.

262
00:22:05,540 --> 00:22:06,370
Don't worry.

263
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:11,410
Sabo!

264
00:22:12,760 --> 00:22:13,840
Here I go!

265
00:22:14,940 --> 00:22:16,881
Watch out for me out there, okay?

266
00:22:20,420 --> 00:22:22,720
Sabo was first, and Ace was second.

267
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:27,177
I may be the last to go, but
I'm going to be the best.

268
00:22:27,260 --> 00:22:28,680
I'm coming for you, Ace.

269
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:31,320
And all my special moves work now, too!

270
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:33,137
Why are you talking to yourself?

271
00:22:33,220 --> 00:22:35,985
Is this some kind of
pirate ritual I don't get?

272
00:22:36,300 --> 00:22:41,420
No, it's a challenge to my brother,
Ace. Ace? Who is that? I don't know.

273
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:44,140
Okay, I'm going for real now.

274
00:22:53,180 --> 00:22:56,280
I knew this day would come,
but I'm still a bit sad.

275
00:22:56,620 --> 00:22:57,738
I'll sure miss him.

276
00:22:58,880 --> 00:23:01,645
Satisfied, like the world
needs another pirate.

277
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:08,440
Oh, perfect weather today. Lock me!

278
00:23:13,340 --> 00:23:14,170
Hey!

279
00:23:21,260 --> 00:23:22,380
Oh, no!

280
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:27,940
Hey, pal.

281
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:29,593
It's been a while, huh?

282
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:37,097
This won't play out like last time.

283
00:23:37,180 --> 00:23:40,760
I've been practicing this
move for ten whole years!

284
00:23:41,480 --> 00:23:43,520
Now, Gon-Gon!

285
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:51,020
Pistol!

286
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:11,840
Been waiting a long time to do that. Yeah!

287
00:24:12,820 --> 00:24:13,650
Yay!

288
00:24:18,260 --> 00:24:22,060
We just took out that
sea monster in one punch.

289
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:26,340
I gotta admit, I'm proud.

290
00:24:27,940 --> 00:24:29,660
First, I need a crew.

291
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:32,440
About ten people should be enough.

292
00:24:33,320 --> 00:24:35,397
After that, pirate flag.

293
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:37,580
All right!

294
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:39,520
Let's get going!

295
00:24:41,840 --> 00:24:43,480
Someday I'm gonna be...

296
00:24:45,300 --> 00:24:47,480
King of the Pirates!

297
00:24:57,600 --> 00:25:00,340
But time has not been kind.

298
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:07,280
And after the death of Ace, Luffy's
optimism from that day is nowhere in sight.

299
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:22,180
Blaze, Luffy.

300
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:25,600
The King of the Pirates!

301
00:25:26,020 --> 00:25:27,337
I'm so...

302
00:25:27,420 --> 00:25:30,080
I'm so weak!

303
00:25:31,100 --> 00:25:31,977
It's Garp!

304
00:25:32,060 --> 00:25:35,640
Garp is back and he brought
his battleship! Should we run?

305
00:25:36,060 --> 00:25:38,817
I read about the battle at
Marineford in the paper.

306
00:25:38,900 --> 00:25:40,782
Congratulations on your victory!

307
00:25:41,160 --> 00:25:43,220
Word travels fast these days, huh?

308
00:25:43,420 --> 00:25:44,280
Is Luffy okay?

309
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:48,037
Now that Whitebeard's dead, the
pirates are going out of control.

310
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:49,377
Is that why you're here?

311
00:25:49,460 --> 00:25:50,813
Things have gotten bad.

312
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:52,137
We're afraid to go out.

313
00:25:52,220 --> 00:25:54,455
They're like vultures staring us down.

314
00:25:55,040 --> 00:25:58,937
I don't mean to complain, but I'm
afraid they can invade any second now.

315
00:25:59,020 --> 00:25:59,850
Not likely.

316
00:25:59,933 --> 00:26:03,406
I just sunk three of them with
cannonballs on the way out here.

317
00:26:04,060 --> 00:26:05,420
Really? Whoa.

318
00:26:06,140 --> 00:26:08,669
They were nothing but
a bunch of blowhards.

319
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:10,140
All bark and no bite.

320
00:26:10,560 --> 00:26:12,677
The seas are going to
be tense the world over

321
00:26:12,760 --> 00:26:15,357
without Whitebeard to
scare off all the thugs.

322
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:18,146
Even if that's not the
Navy's official stance.

323
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:23,900
Anyway, since you're so far from our base,
I prepared a little something. See? Sir!

324
00:26:26,080 --> 00:26:28,177
Security by Navy Vice Admiral Garp?

325
00:26:28,260 --> 00:26:30,220
That'll scare them off for sure.

326
00:26:30,520 --> 00:26:33,402
One look at that and
they'll straighten right up.

327
00:26:33,700 --> 00:26:36,288
While you're here,
there's one more problem.

328
00:26:36,440 --> 00:26:38,937
A bunch of mountain bandits
came down to the village.

329
00:26:39,020 --> 00:26:41,877
They took over Maki-no's
bar and they aren't leaving.

330
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:42,790
That's all.

331
00:26:43,480 --> 00:26:45,020
Please, calm down!

332
00:26:49,860 --> 00:26:50,980
Hello, Garp.

333
00:26:51,180 --> 00:26:52,827
Hey, that's one right there.

334
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:56,537
How dare you show your face here?

335
00:26:56,620 --> 00:26:58,100
After what you've done!

336
00:26:59,340 --> 00:27:02,277
Garp That's not good.

337
00:27:02,360 --> 00:27:03,540
Var General

338
00:27:09,840 --> 00:27:11,497
Back off, man!

339
00:27:11,580 --> 00:27:12,877
She's a friend.

340
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:17,620
The hell I am!

341
00:27:18,340 --> 00:27:20,987
You were right with them
on that battlefield?

342
00:27:22,040 --> 00:27:25,720
Those poor boys and you didn't
do a damn thing to help them!

343
00:27:25,960 --> 00:27:28,019
Why did you have me raise ace, huh?

344
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:32,340
Why did you have me take care of
them if it was good in this way?

345
00:27:40,820 --> 00:27:43,600
You stood there and watched that boy die!

346
00:27:44,580 --> 00:27:47,997
You care more about your
damn job than your family!

347
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:50,220
The great hero of the Navy!

348
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:53,637
I hope you're proud of yourself,
you heartless piece of crap!

349
00:27:53,720 --> 00:27:54,960
Now, now, boss!

350
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:56,300
Take it easy!

351
00:27:56,980 --> 00:27:58,700
Say something, you bastard!

352
00:27:59,080 --> 00:28:00,417
Why didn't you help him?

353
00:28:00,500 --> 00:28:02,147
Why didn't you do something?

354
00:28:03,260 --> 00:28:06,740
Look me right in the face,
you spineless wretch!

355
00:28:06,900 --> 00:28:08,400
You answer me, dammit!

356
00:28:09,380 --> 00:28:10,620
Dejan, enough!

357
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:18,140
Knock it out.

358
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:38,257
How do you think he feels?

359
00:28:38,340 --> 00:28:39,557
He's their grandfather.

360
00:28:39,640 --> 00:28:40,800
He's suffering too.

361
00:28:41,100 --> 00:28:43,747
He was right there and
he couldn't do a thing

362
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:55,480
You're wrong.

363
00:28:57,500 --> 00:28:58,900
Garp is suffering.

364
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:01,270
No.

365
00:29:03,120 --> 00:29:07,020
The only one who's really
suffering here is Luffy damn it.

366
00:29:17,040 --> 00:29:20,393
Okay, so let's pretend Shanks
is here with you right now.

367
00:29:20,540 --> 00:29:21,481
What do you say?

368
00:29:22,140 --> 00:29:23,540
Hi, I'm Ace.

369
00:29:23,780 --> 00:29:25,520
Who the hell are you? Boo!

370
00:29:25,960 --> 00:29:29,377
I know you're pirates, but I
don't think he'd be impressed.

371
00:29:29,460 --> 00:29:30,290
Yeah!

372
00:29:30,373 --> 00:29:31,220
Be way more cool!

373
00:29:33,180 --> 00:29:35,340
Fancy meeting you here. Boo!

374
00:29:36,220 --> 00:29:38,540
Mister, what's your deal? Boo.

375
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:41,520
Because he didn't say punk?

376
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:42,920
Nope, nope.

377
00:29:44,220 --> 00:29:45,540
Luffy, stop.

378
00:29:45,880 --> 00:29:47,527
You're distracting poor Ace.

379
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:49,217
Go be stupid somewhere else.

380
00:29:49,300 --> 00:29:50,177
We're learning here.

381
00:29:50,260 --> 00:29:51,280
You little pest.

382
00:29:51,600 --> 00:29:52,776
I'm not distracting.

383
00:29:53,060 --> 00:29:53,920
Oh, yeah.

384
00:29:54,220 --> 00:29:58,237
I found an anaconda nest filled with a
bunch of eggs and they're super huge.

385
00:29:58,320 --> 00:29:59,917
Let's grab them and cook them up.

386
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:00,830
What?

387
00:30:00,913 --> 00:30:02,091
Man, that sounds awesome.

388
00:30:02,380 --> 00:30:03,480
No, not right now.

389
00:30:04,640 --> 00:30:07,257
I'm gonna learn some
manners even if it kills me.

390
00:30:07,340 --> 00:30:08,780
I can't go on my own.

391
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:10,980
What if the anaconda mom finds me?

392
00:30:11,220 --> 00:30:13,857
But if you're there with
me, we can beat it for sure.

393
00:30:13,940 --> 00:30:14,770
Come on, let's go.

394
00:30:14,853 --> 00:30:15,683
I said no.

395
00:30:19,020 --> 00:30:21,844
Luffy loved Ace more than
anything in the world.

396
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:32,830
Ragino.

397
00:30:36,040 --> 00:30:36,920
Hey, Garp.

398
00:30:37,620 --> 00:30:39,120
What happened to Luffy?

399
00:30:39,300 --> 00:30:42,182
The newspaper said he went
missing after the war.

400
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:43,380
That he did.

401
00:30:49,760 --> 00:30:51,920
The submarine carried him away.

402
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:56,652
The admirals attacked and tried
to stop him from escaping,

403
00:30:56,840 --> 00:30:58,837
and afterwards they held a search.

404
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:01,567
But they couldn't find
a single trace of him.

405
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:05,900
There was no shipwreck,
so he's probably alive.

406
00:31:07,380 --> 00:31:08,520
That's a relief.

407
00:31:08,720 --> 00:31:10,697
Wait, so what's up with this bandit?

408
00:31:10,780 --> 00:31:14,917
She obviously seems to know Garp, but
why did he let her punch him like that?

409
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:15,830
Yeah.

410
00:31:21,640 --> 00:31:24,537
Luffy's been a little moron
since the day I met him.

411
00:31:24,620 --> 00:31:28,000
But no matter what he does,
I'm always on his side.

412
00:31:30,860 --> 00:31:34,120
As much as I'm hurting,
I know he's got it worse.

413
00:31:34,380 --> 00:31:36,020
And it breaks my heart.

414
00:31:46,520 --> 00:31:52,400
I know things are hard right
now, but don't you dare give up!

415
00:31:57,820 --> 00:32:04,080
Meanwhile, far away and far along the Grand
Line, in a place known as the New World,

416
00:32:32,820 --> 00:32:35,467
I don't know how I can
ever thank you enough.

417
00:32:37,340 --> 00:32:39,516
No need to make a big deal out of it.

418
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:44,038
Whitebeard was a rival, but I still
held a lot of respect for the man.

419
00:32:44,980 --> 00:32:46,860
Even Sengoku felt that way.

420
00:32:49,420 --> 00:32:51,940
Well, I suppose it's time for us to go.

421
00:32:52,680 --> 00:32:53,974
Yeah, thank you again.

422
00:32:55,360 --> 00:32:58,400
I can only imagine how
tough this is on Luffy.

423
00:32:59,700 --> 00:33:03,360
Even so, his brother died like a true man.

424
00:33:04,820 --> 00:33:07,200
Take it back, or else.

425
00:33:07,340 --> 00:33:10,980
You don't know anything about
the man who saved my life!

426
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:12,560
This is his era!

427
00:33:12,860 --> 00:33:14,320
Don't you forget it!

428
00:33:19,800 --> 00:33:22,000
Maybe Ace wouldn't want to hear this,

429
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:25,376
but that's exactly what
Captain Roger would have done.

430
00:33:27,060 --> 00:33:31,360
There were times when I wished
he wasn't too bold to run away.

431
00:33:33,340 --> 00:33:35,200
Too bold to shed tears.

432
00:33:41,440 --> 00:33:47,260
Listen, Luffy, it's not only victory
that makes a man, but defeat,

433
00:33:47,740 --> 00:33:49,540
joy and sorrow alike.

434
00:33:50,340 --> 00:33:52,600
There's no shame in backing down.

435
00:34:02,940 --> 00:34:04,740
There's no shame in crying.

436
00:34:07,360 --> 00:34:09,820
So long as you overcome it.

437
00:34:25,240 --> 00:34:26,180
Dammit!

438
00:34:26,440 --> 00:34:29,300
I couldn't save my crew or my brother!

439
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:31,300
Luffy...

440
00:34:32,340 --> 00:34:33,520
Go away!

441
00:34:34,580 --> 00:34:36,280
Leave me alone!

442
00:34:37,340 --> 00:34:38,170
I cannot.

443
00:34:38,380 --> 00:34:43,086
Although I understand your pain, I will
not allow you to hurt yourself any more.

444
00:34:44,140 --> 00:34:45,493
It's not your business!

445
00:34:45,800 --> 00:34:47,220
This is my body!

446
00:34:47,560 --> 00:34:48,619
What of Ace, then?

447
00:34:48,820 --> 00:34:51,440
Who sacrificed his body to protect you?

448
00:34:51,840 --> 00:34:53,664
Was that none of your business?

449
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:55,780
You bastard! Shut up!

450
00:34:55,960 --> 00:34:58,540
Say one more word and I'm gonna crush you!

451
00:34:58,860 --> 00:35:01,877
If that would make you happy,
then why don't you try?

452
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:04,120
But let me warn you injured though.

453
00:35:04,280 --> 00:35:07,520
I am you will not defeat
me not in that condition

454
00:35:36,160 --> 00:35:37,700
Let me tell you something.

455
00:35:38,900 --> 00:35:41,760
A while back, when I
was hunting down Teach,

456
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:48,740
I went to Alabasta Kingdom, and I saw my
brother for the first time in three years.

457
00:35:49,560 --> 00:35:53,620
As soon as I saw his face, a
weight lifted from my heart.

458
00:35:55,100 --> 00:35:56,500
And do you know why?

459
00:36:02,540 --> 00:36:03,370
Ow!

460
00:36:03,453 --> 00:36:04,340
Are you insane?

461
00:36:04,600 --> 00:36:05,700
Stop moving!

462
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:09,441
I've had enough of your nonsense!

463
00:36:15,720 --> 00:36:18,620
Boy, you can't see a thing. You're blind.

464
00:36:19,380 --> 00:36:21,262
You never doubted your strength.

465
00:36:21,420 --> 00:36:22,320
But now,

466
00:36:22,500 --> 00:36:26,657
the confidence that once allowed you to
soar above the clouds has been shattered.

467
00:36:26,740 --> 00:36:30,017
Your brother who was your
guiding light has faded away.

468
00:36:30,100 --> 00:36:33,937
and your enemy stands so
tall and casts so great a

469
00:36:34,020 --> 00:36:37,297
shadow that you can do naught
but cower in the darkness.

470
00:36:37,380 --> 00:36:42,440
And now, you strike out like an animal at
the cage your doubt has placed around you.

471
00:36:44,780 --> 00:36:47,740
So long as you are consumed
by regret and guilt,

472
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:50,176
you will never find your way forward.

473
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:56,000
Luffy, your pain may be great,
but it mustn't devour you.

474
00:36:56,740 --> 00:36:59,300
There is yet joy beyond your sorrows.

475
00:37:00,100 --> 00:37:01,580
What's gone may be gone,

476
00:37:01,860 --> 00:37:06,036
but you still have something left in
this world to treasure, don't you?

477
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:57,377
Hey, if you want to screw
around, go do it somewhere else.

478
00:37:57,460 --> 00:37:59,342
I'm trying to build muscle here.

479
00:38:04,400 --> 00:38:05,230
Luffy!

480
00:38:05,340 --> 00:38:07,516
We've got a big storm on the horizon!

481
00:38:07,680 --> 00:38:09,151
Make preparations, quick!

482
00:38:10,800 --> 00:38:12,140
I had a big one.

483
00:38:12,280 --> 00:38:13,357
You just missed it.

484
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:16,060
But the next one is
going to be even bigger.

485
00:38:19,660 --> 00:38:20,490
Scram.

486
00:38:20,573 --> 00:38:21,420
I'm almost done.

487
00:38:21,740 --> 00:38:23,152
Just keep your pants on.

488
00:38:24,140 --> 00:38:24,980
It's okay.

489
00:38:25,240 --> 00:38:27,797
No matter how bad you're
hurt, you're in good hands.

490
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:30,640
By the way, this one
might sting a little bit.

491
00:38:35,060 --> 00:38:36,340
Oh, Luffy.

492
00:38:36,780 --> 00:38:40,460
If you like treasure, this
research is fascinating. Come see.

493
00:38:43,880 --> 00:38:44,880
What's up, buddy?

494
00:38:45,140 --> 00:38:48,611
If you're checking on the coal
engine, it's in super shape.

495
00:38:49,380 --> 00:38:52,440
And if you're checking on
me, well, I'm super too.

496
00:38:52,800 --> 00:38:54,976
Good morning, Captain Rise and Shine.

497
00:38:55,340 --> 00:38:57,237
How about I play you a little song?

498
00:38:57,320 --> 00:38:59,360
to really get those bones moving.

499
00:39:08,040 --> 00:39:19,100
Luffy.

500
00:39:19,860 --> 00:39:21,000
Captain Luffy!

501
00:39:22,080 --> 00:39:23,100
Luffy!

502
00:39:35,520 --> 00:39:36,720
My crew.

503
00:39:37,620 --> 00:39:39,920
I still have my crew.

504
00:39:40,480 --> 00:39:46,900
Zoro, Nami, Usopp, Sanji, Jumper,
Robin, Franky, and Brooke.

505
00:39:47,300 --> 00:39:49,900
They're still out there waiting for me.

506
00:39:51,940 --> 00:39:53,480
Now do you see?

507
00:39:54,420 --> 00:39:58,185
I have to get back to this ship,
no matter how long it takes me.

508
00:39:58,760 --> 00:40:02,660
Guys, meet back on the
sunny in three days! Roger!

509
00:40:05,100 --> 00:40:07,840
Everything's a mess, and I'm already late.

510
00:40:08,040 --> 00:40:10,600
But I have to make it back to Sabahodi.

511
00:40:10,980 --> 00:40:12,420
I know they'll be there.

512
00:40:13,440 --> 00:40:18,160
It wasn't just knowing he was
safe, or seeing him smile again.

513
00:40:20,740 --> 00:40:26,540
When you've got a bungling kid brother
like me, you can't help but worry a bit.

514
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:33,264
He might be a bit much for all of you to
handle, but take good care of him for me.

515
00:40:34,380 --> 00:40:38,560
I mean, sure, he wasn't the snot-nosed
kid following me around anymore,

516
00:40:38,900 --> 00:40:42,220
but more than that, he had friends.

517
00:40:45,380 --> 00:40:47,740
